@workspace twixy

SKILL "YouTube Transcript"
  version: 1.5
  description: "Open a YouTube video, handle ads, open the transcript panel, and extract the full transcript text. Falls back to description + chapter timestamps if the transcript is unavailable."
  tags: [youtube, transcript, captions, video, browser, data-collection]

PLATFORMS {
  YOUTUBE
}

GOAL "Extract YouTube transcript or chapter outline" {
  objective: "Given a YouTube video URL, retrieve a usable text representation of the video's content — preferred order: full transcript → auto-generated captions → description + chapter timestamps. Save the result to disk so downstream skills can consume it."
  kpi: transcript_chars_extracted
}

COLLECT "Open the video and prepare the page" {
  USE youtube WITH profile = "twixy" AS yt

  🚨 "Twixy" is THIS APP'S NAME — NOT a YouTube channel or username. NEVER search "twixy" on YouTube and NEVER navigate to youtube.com/@twixy.
  🚨 You are a sub-agent. Run all browser calls yourself directly. Do NOT spawn further sub-agents.
  Always use lowercase profile: "twixy" for all browser calls. Capital "T" is wrong and will fail.
  browser status running: false does NOT mean the page failed — cookies and session persist in the twixy profile.

  Required input: $videoUrl — a full YouTube watch URL (e.g. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID).

  PHASE 1 — Open the video and capture metadata:

  Step 1: Open $videoUrl with browser open profile=twixy. Save the returned targetId as $tab.

  Step 2: Wait 1.5 seconds — browser act kind=wait timeMs=1500 — let the player and metadata initialize.

  Step 3: Capture video metadata via the player API. Pass the function as-is, no extra escaping.
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { try { const p = document.getElementById("movie_player"); if (!p || !p.getVideoData) return { error: "no player" }; const d = p.getVideoData(); const r = p.getPlayerResponse ? p.getPlayerResponse() : null; const dur = (r && r.videoDetails && Number(r.videoDetails.lengthSeconds)) || (p.getDuration && p.getDuration()) || null; return { videoId: d.video_id, title: d.title, lengthSeconds: dur, author: d.author }; } catch(e) { return { error: String(e) }; } }'
    → Save the result as $meta. The lengthSeconds field is the SOURCE OF TRUTH for video length.
    🚨 DO NOT infer video length from the URL `t=` parameter — that is a START TIME, not a duration. Confusing the two leads to wrong assumptions.
}

EXECUTE "Wait out any pre-roll ad before interacting" {
  PHASE 2 — Ad handling:

  ⚠️ KNOWN ISSUE — needs more work. The current skip-button click is unreliable: `.ytp-ad-skip-button*` selectors miss several real-world ad variants and on multiple recent runs the agent reported "clicked" while the ad continued playing — the user had to skip manually. Treat this section as best-effort until the selector list is widened, the inner <button> drill-down is applied (like Phase 3), and a post-click `.ad-showing` clearing check is added.

  An ad blocks the player UI and the description "...more" button cannot be clicked while it is on screen. Always settle the ad first.

  Step 1: Probe ad state.
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const adShowing = document.querySelector(".ad-showing") !== null || document.querySelector(".ytp-ad-player-overlay") !== null || document.querySelector(".ytp-ad-text") !== null; const skipBtn = document.querySelector(".ytp-ad-skip-button, .ytp-ad-skip-button-modern, button.ytp-skip-ad-button"); return { adShowing, hasSkipButton: !!skipBtn }; }'

  Step 2: If adShowing is false → ad already finished. Skip to Phase 3.

  Step 3: If hasSkipButton is true → click it.
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const b = document.querySelector(".ytp-ad-skip-button, .ytp-ad-skip-button-modern, button.ytp-skip-ad-button"); if (b) { b.click(); return "clicked"; } return "no-button"; }'
    Then wait 1 second and re-probe.

  Step 4: If skip button is not yet clickable → poll up to 30 seconds, checking ad state every 2 seconds. Use evaluate, NOT snapshot — snapshots of the player overlay are large and ad-heavy.
    Loop: browser act kind=wait timeMs=2000 → re-probe Step 1 → break when adShowing is false OR hasSkipButton becomes true (then click it).

  Step 5: If 30 seconds elapse and the ad is still showing → record a warning and continue anyway. The transcript flow may still work because the description column is below the player and partially independent.

  🚨 NEVER take a full-page snapshot during an ad. The overlay produces tens of thousands of irrelevant tokens.
}

EXECUTE "Open the transcript panel and extract segments" {
  PHASE 3 — Open transcript:

  YouTube's transcript button lives inside the description's "...more" expansion, not next to the player.

  Step 1: Expand the description.
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const btn = document.querySelector("tp-yt-paper-button#expand, ytd-text-inline-expander #expand"); if (btn) { btn.click(); return "expanded"; } return "no-expand-button"; }'
    Wait 800ms — browser act kind=wait timeMs=800.

  Step 2: Click the "Show transcript" button by EXACT visible text — but cover ALL major YouTube UI locales. The user's browser language determines the label, so the regex MUST include English + Korean + Japanese + Chinese (Simp/Trad) + Spanish + Portuguese + French + German + Italian + Russian + Vietnamese + Indonesian + Thai + Hindi + Arabic. Do NOT match the bare localized word for "transcript" — every locale's description column also contains a heading and a "follow along" sentence whose text includes that word, and loose matching clicks one of those (silent failure → 6 polls of 0 → forced Phase 4). EXACT anchor `^...$` only.
    🚨 If the user's locale isn't in the list, fall through to Phase 4 rather than guessing — never expand the list at runtime.
    🚨 Click ONCE only. A second click on the SAME button toggles the panel closed — never re-click; if the first click didn't take, fall through to Phase 4.
    🚨 Inside the fn body, use SINGLE quotes for every selector string. The fn is passed as a double-quoted JSON string, so '[class*="x"]' inside double quotes corrupts into a SyntaxError.
    🚨 YouTube renders the description transcript section TWICE in the DOM — both instances contain identical `aria-label="Show transcript"` buttons with identical text. Only one is laid out and active in the current variant; the other is hidden/detached. A naive `candidates.find(...)` returns the first DOM match (often the hidden copy), `btn.click()` succeeds but YouTube ignores the event, and `engagement-panel-searchable-transcript` stays HIDDEN forever. Filter candidates with `el.offsetParent !== null && getBoundingClientRect()` size > 0 BEFORE picking — visible-in-layout only.
    🚨 Each button is THREE nested elements: `ytd-button-renderer > yt-button-shape > <button>`. innerText cascades so all three wrappers pass the locale regex (matchCount becomes `3 × instances`, typically 6). Calling `.click()` on the outer `ytd-button-renderer` or `yt-button-shape` does NOT trigger YouTube's click handler — that handler is bound to the innermost native `<button>`. After picking the visible candidate, drill into its `<button>` descendant via `candidate.querySelector("button")` before clicking. Log `clickedTag` to verify — it must be "button".
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const isClickable = el => { if (!el) return false; const tag = el.tagName.toLowerCase(); if (tag === "button") return true; if (el.getAttribute("role") === "button") return true; if (tag === "yt-button-shape" || tag === "ytd-button-renderer") return true; return false; }; const isVisible = el => { if (el.offsetParent === null) return false; const r = el.getBoundingClientRect(); return r.width > 0 && r.height > 0; }; const labelRe = /^(show transcript|자막 표시|스크립트 표시|文字起こしを表示|显示转写文字|显示文字记录|顯示文字轉錄|mostrar transcripción|mostrar transcrição|afficher la transcription|transkript anzeigen|mostra trascrizione|показать расшифровку|hiển thị bản chép lời|tampilkan transkrip|แสดงคำบรรยาย|ट्रांसक्रिप्ट दिखाएं|عرض النص)$/i; const matches = [...document.querySelectorAll("button, [role=\"button\"], yt-button-shape, ytd-button-renderer")].filter(el => isClickable(el)).filter(el => labelRe.test((el.innerText || el.textContent || "").trim())); const candidate = matches.find(isVisible); if (!candidate) return { clicked: false, reason: matches.length ? "all-candidates-hidden" : "no-transcript-button-in-known-locale", matchCount: matches.length }; const realBtn = candidate.tagName.toLowerCase() === "button" ? candidate : (candidate.querySelector("button") || candidate); const panelBefore = document.querySelector("ytd-transcript-panel-renderer, ytd-engagement-panel-section-list-renderer[target-id=\"engagement-panel-searchable-transcript\"]"); const segCountBefore = document.querySelectorAll("ytd-transcript-segment-renderer").length; realBtn.click(); return { clicked: true, label: (realBtn.innerText || realBtn.textContent || "").trim(), clickedTag: realBtn.tagName.toLowerCase(), matchCount: matches.length, panelBefore: !!panelBefore, segCountBefore }; }'
    → If clicked is false, skip to Phase 4. The reason field distinguishes "no locale match" (matchCount 0) from "all matches hidden" (matchCount > 0). Verify `clickedTag === "button"` in the result; if it's "ytd-button-renderer" or "yt-button-shape", the drill-down failed and the click likely did not register. Otherwise note segCountBefore for the panel-state check below.

  Step 3: 🚨 CRITICAL — Transcript segments are LAZY-LOADED. The panel renders empty for 1–3 seconds before segments appear. DO NOT treat an empty panel as failure on the first read.

  🚨 The Step 2 click is already validated — the regex is anchored `^...$` against a known locale label list, so `clicked: true` proves the right button was hit. DO NOT use panel-presence as a wrong-click signal: the transcript panel is rendered under different parent tags depending on YouTube layout (`ytd-transcript-panel-renderer` vs `ytd-engagement-panel-section-list-renderer[target-id="engagement-panel-searchable-transcript"]`), and a single-selector miss is a *false negative*, not a wrong click.

  Poll ONLY on segment count, up to 6 attempts at 800ms intervals (~5 seconds total). Panel info is diagnostic-only — log it but do NOT branch on it.
    Loop (i = 1..6):
      browser act kind=wait timeMs=800
      browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const panel = document.querySelector("ytd-transcript-panel-renderer, ytd-engagement-panel-section-list-renderer[target-id=\"engagement-panel-searchable-transcript\"]"); return { panelPresent: !!panel, panelHidden: panel ? (panel.hasAttribute("hidden") || panel.getAttribute("visibility") === "ENGAGEMENT_PANEL_VISIBILITY_HIDDEN") : null, segCount: document.querySelectorAll("ytd-transcript-segment-renderer").length }; }'
      → Break when segCount > 0.
      → If still 0 segments after attempt 6 → Phase 4. The video genuinely has no captions.

  Step 4: Extract all segments in ONE evaluate call. Do NOT loop tool calls per segment.
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const segs = [...document.querySelectorAll("ytd-transcript-segment-renderer")]; if (!segs.length) return { segments: [], note: "empty" }; const out = segs.map(s => { const ts = s.querySelector(".segment-timestamp, [class*=\"timestamp\"]")?.innerText?.trim() || ""; const tx = s.querySelector(".segment-text, yt-formatted-string.segment-text, [class*=\"segment-text\"]")?.innerText?.trim() || ""; return { ts, text: tx }; }).filter(x => x.text); return { segments: out, count: out.length }; }'
    → Save as $segments. Combine into plain text: "[ts] text" per line.

  STORE $segments AS "youtube_transcript_{videoId}_{date}" IN $RAW
}

ANALYZE "Fallback to description + chapter timestamps" {
  PHASE 4 — Run ONLY if Phase 3 returned 0 segments after polling.

  Many videos lack captions or block timedtext API access from automation. Description + chapters is the reliable secondary signal.

  Step 1: Make sure the description is expanded (re-run Phase 3 Step 1 if needed).

  Step 2: Extract chapter timestamps and the full description text.
    browser act kind=evaluate fn='() => { const desc = document.querySelector("ytd-text-inline-expander, #description-inline-expander, ytd-watch-metadata #description")?.innerText?.trim() || ""; const chapEls = [...document.querySelectorAll("ytd-macro-markers-list-item-renderer, [class*=\"chapter\"], [id*=\"chapter\"]")]; const chapters = chapEls.map(el => { const ts = el.querySelector("#time, [class*=\"time\"]")?.innerText?.trim() || ""; const tx = el.querySelector("#title, h4, [class*=\"title\"]")?.innerText?.trim() || ""; return { ts, title: tx }; }).filter(c => c.ts && c.title); return { description: desc, chapters }; }'
    → Save as $fallback.

  Step 3: 🚨 DO NOT use web_fetch on the youtube.com/api/timedtext URL. The signed caption URL is bound to the player's IP/session and returns empty when fetched server-side. Multiple retries on this endpoint are a known waste pattern — skip it entirely.

  STORE $fallback AS "youtube_description_{videoId}_{date}" IN $RAW
}

TRACK "Save final artifact and report" {
  LOAD "youtube_transcript_{videoId}_{date}" FROM $RAW AS $transcript
  IF MISSING $transcript → LOAD "youtube_description_{videoId}_{date}" FROM $RAW AS $transcript

  🚨 RAW VERBATIM ONLY. This skill captures ground-truth text — NOT a summary. Forbidden:
    - Combining adjacent segments into "paragraphs" or "sentences"
    - Inventing section headings like "### 0:00 ~ 0:42 — 소개"
    - Bullet-point summaries of what was said
    - Translation, transliteration, or "cleaned-up" punctuation
    - Any commentary, opinion, or framing
    - Skipping segments because they look redundant
  Summarization belongs to the NEXT skill or workflow node in the plan, never this one. The raw file must exist independently so other consumers (and the user) can re-derive different views of it later. A previous run extracted 237 segments perfectly, then wrote a 5KB hand-summarized guide instead — the user could not tell from the file whether captions had been captured. Do not repeat that.

  Build a single markdown artifact in this EXACT layout:
    # {title}

    **URL:** {watch URL}
    **Channel:** {author}
    **Duration:** {lengthSeconds}s
    **Extracted:** {date}
    **Source:** transcript    ← or "description-fallback"

    ---

    [0:00] {first segment text exactly as captured}
    [0:01] {second segment text exactly as captured}
    [0:03] {third segment text exactly as captured}
    ... (continue for ALL segments — do NOT skip, merge, or rewrite)

  For the fallback path (no captions), the body after `---` becomes the raw `description` text followed by a `## Chapters` block listing `[ts] title` lines verbatim.

  Save to ~/.openclaw/workspace/twixy/data/raw/youtube_{videoId}_{date}.md using the write_file tool.
  🚨 Filename pattern is exactly `youtube_{videoId}_{date}.md` — no `_transcript` or other suffix.

  Report to the user (or parent skill) in this exact shape:
    [transcript] Extracted {N} segments from "{title}" — saved to {path}
  OR if fallback was used:
    [transcript-fallback] Captions unavailable for "{title}". Extracted description + {C} chapters — saved to {path}

  EMIT "transcript_ready"
    WITH payload = { videoId, source, path, charCount }
    TO SKILL "Analytics"
}
